WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:44.087
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:44.357 --> 00:48.069
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

3
00:51.781 --> 00:54.701
‎"However, the patient died ‎two months after the surgery."

4
00:56.703 --> 00:58.580
‎"The cause of death remains unknown."

5
00:59.706 --> 01:03.710
‎"When asked by a reporter ‎about filing a malpractice suit,

6
01:03.793 --> 01:06.171
‎the bereaved family declined to comment."

7
01:25.857 --> 01:28.234
‎"The surgeon's name was not revealed."

8
01:28.943 --> 01:30.904
‎"But the pseudonym in the chart was

9
01:30.987 --> 01:32.488
‎Doctor X."

10
01:32.572 --> 01:33.865
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

11
01:35.033 --> 01:36.993
‎Dr. Gye, are you okay?

12
01:40.288 --> 01:41.122
‎Are you okay?

13
01:47.503 --> 01:51.674
‎EPISODE 3

14
01:52.216 --> 01:53.176
‎So…

15
01:54.010 --> 01:56.846
‎Are you saying Dr. Gye is Doctor X?

16
01:58.389 --> 02:00.350
‎Look at the photo description here.

17
02:01.059 --> 02:03.228
‎It says, "the surgical team."

18
02:03.311 --> 02:05.980
‎There is one Asian person ‎wearing a white coat.

19
02:07.190 --> 02:08.650
‎Why is it so blurry?

20
02:09.901 --> 02:11.194
‎Dr. Bae.

21
02:11.903 --> 02:14.113
‎This is just a rumor.

22
02:14.197 --> 02:15.198
‎You believe this?

23
02:16.074 --> 02:17.909
‎What we're trying to say is

24
02:17.992 --> 02:19.953
‎there's a problem with the procedure.

25
02:20.036 --> 02:22.956
‎If Dr. Gye followed this procedure,

26
02:23.039 --> 02:26.876
‎the chances of our patient ‎ending up like this in two months…

27
02:27.961 --> 02:29.796
‎That's all the more reason ‎we can't let her go.

28
02:31.297 --> 02:34.175
‎If things go wrong, ‎someone has to take the fall.

29
02:35.093 --> 02:36.261
‎The primary surgeon

30
02:37.679 --> 02:39.514
‎was you, Dr. Do, after all.

31
02:46.479 --> 02:47.605
‎Her contract

32
02:48.147 --> 02:49.941
‎doesn't specify any department.

33
02:50.024 --> 02:51.693
‎Director, does that mean…

34
02:54.320 --> 02:56.280
‎Let's call Dr. Gye in here.

35
02:56.864 --> 02:58.408
‎Oh, the thing is…

36
02:59.200 --> 03:00.994
‎She hasn't come to work yet.

37
03:03.079 --> 03:04.580
‎We just got to work, Ms. Jang.

38
03:05.331 --> 03:06.249
‎Good morning.

39
03:07.041 --> 03:08.334
‎You're greeting her in English?

40
03:08.918 --> 03:10.795
‎-Ohayo. ‎-Look at you.

41
03:10.878 --> 03:12.755
‎-What else? ‎-Ciao!

42
03:13.256 --> 03:16.092
‎I'm memorizing morning greetings ‎to prevent dementia.

43
03:16.175 --> 03:17.885
‎-You're so silly. ‎-Hey, move.

44
03:17.969 --> 03:19.679
‎-I need to go. ‎-Why?

45
03:21.431 --> 03:23.766
‎Su-jeong hasn't gone in to work.

46
03:23.850 --> 03:25.393
‎-She's not answering either. ‎-What?

47
03:25.476 --> 03:27.437
‎She must be at home then. ‎Where else could she be?

48
03:27.520 --> 03:30.064
‎She's obviously not home. ‎Let's look for her too.

49
03:30.148 --> 03:31.107
‎Hold on.

50
03:31.691 --> 03:32.650
‎Hey, you punk!

51
03:33.234 --> 03:35.695
‎What are you doing? ‎Why aren't you at work yet?

52
03:35.778 --> 03:37.739
‎Jo Won-jin? Who's that?

53
03:37.822 --> 03:39.991
‎Why are you answering Su-jeong's… Oh my.

54
03:40.950 --> 03:41.909
‎Dr. Jo.

55
03:42.702 --> 03:45.830
‎Of course, I know you. ‎You're the attending anesthesiologist.

56
03:47.373 --> 03:48.833
‎Dr. Gye is in the ER?

57
03:51.544 --> 03:53.171
‎So she did make it to work.

58
03:56.799 --> 03:58.509
‎Things could have been worse.

59
03:59.260 --> 04:01.012
‎Yes, and we performed ‎a transfusion quickly.

60
04:01.095 --> 04:01.929
‎Dr. Gye.

61
04:04.015 --> 04:04.932
‎Dr. Gye?

62
04:05.516 --> 04:06.392
‎I'm sorry.

63
04:07.060 --> 04:09.604
‎-What exactly did he think I said? ‎-Dr. Gye?

64
04:09.687 --> 04:11.314
‎What? Is he a doctor too?

65
04:11.397 --> 04:13.858
‎He's an intern, ‎despite looking like a clueless fool.

66
04:15.026 --> 04:16.069
‎Dr. Park Tae-gyeong.

67
04:17.528 --> 04:18.363
‎Dr. Jo.

68
04:19.155 --> 04:21.032
‎Please save Dr. Gye.

69
04:21.115 --> 04:22.742
‎Please save her.

70
04:22.825 --> 04:23.659
‎Dr. Park.

71
04:24.452 --> 04:27.121
‎I think you misunderstood ‎what I said over the phone.

72
04:27.205 --> 04:28.539
‎No, I understood.

73
04:28.623 --> 04:30.750
‎I can give her a transfusion. ‎I have healthy blood.

74
04:30.833 --> 04:32.335
‎You definitely misunderstood.

75
04:32.418 --> 04:34.921
‎The future of Korean medicine ‎is bright and promising.

76
04:35.588 --> 04:38.091
‎-Dr. Gye is lying down here. ‎-Here?

77
04:38.174 --> 04:39.175
‎-She's… ‎-Hey.

78
04:42.929 --> 04:43.805
‎Dr. Gye.

79
04:44.430 --> 04:45.681
‎It's me, Tae-gyeong.

80
04:47.183 --> 04:48.351
‎Oh no.

81
04:49.519 --> 04:52.647
‎Sir, please save Dr. Gye.

82
04:52.730 --> 04:54.357
‎Please save her!

83
04:54.440 --> 04:56.150
‎I'm the one who needs saving.

84
04:57.443 --> 04:59.320
‎-Which department? ‎-Not anesthesiology.

85
04:59.404 --> 05:00.488
‎Thankfully.

86
05:00.571 --> 05:02.990
‎Dr. Gye, please wake up!

87
05:03.074 --> 05:04.575
‎You're the one who needs to wake up.

88
05:04.659 --> 05:06.953
‎Do something about him ‎before he performs CPR.

89
05:07.036 --> 05:08.621
‎What are you doing?

90
05:08.704 --> 05:10.498
‎How did you even become an intern?

91
05:11.165 --> 05:12.083
‎Hello, sir.

92
05:14.794 --> 05:16.504
‎Gosh, not again.

93
05:20.341 --> 05:23.219
‎1 HOUR AGO

94
05:25.304 --> 05:26.514
‎Is the blood ready?

95
05:26.597 --> 05:28.933
‎Not yet. There's been a blood shortage.

96
05:29.016 --> 05:30.601
‎-Blood type? ‎-It's AB.

97
05:30.685 --> 05:32.770
‎Does anyone have any? Damn it.

98
05:32.854 --> 05:35.440
‎-Someone get some AB here! ‎-I'm type AB.

99
05:35.523 --> 05:36.524
‎I'll take her.

100
05:38.651 --> 05:39.610
‎She has a few abrasions.

101
05:39.694 --> 05:41.946
‎-She cried herself to sleep. ‎-Got it.

102
05:42.029 --> 05:43.447
‎You're bleeding too.

103
05:43.531 --> 05:46.242
‎Oh, it's not mine. Let's do this.

104
05:47.577 --> 05:49.704
‎-Please prepare for a transfusion. ‎-Yes, Doctor.

105
05:49.787 --> 05:51.873
‎Dr. Gye, did you eat breakfast?

106
05:51.956 --> 05:52.832
‎A lot.

107
05:54.250 --> 05:55.626
‎What are you doing?

108
05:55.710 --> 05:57.837
‎We're losing blood faster ‎than we're losing time.

109
05:59.964 --> 06:02.216
‎She said something that cool?

110
06:02.800 --> 06:03.885
‎No way.

111
06:03.968 --> 06:06.095
‎It sure doesn't look like it.

112
06:07.346 --> 06:10.433
‎Am I the only one who hears her snoring?

113
06:10.516 --> 06:11.642
‎Sometimes…

114
06:14.520 --> 06:18.232
‎when Dr. Gye speaks normally, ‎there's this strange vibe.

115
06:18.774 --> 06:19.734
‎I know what you mean.

116
06:19.817 --> 06:22.361
‎You noticed it too. So did I. Wow.

117
06:22.445 --> 06:24.405
‎"Wow," my foot. Be quiet.

118
06:24.488 --> 06:27.283
‎Cut it out, everyone. ‎We've got a patient here.

119
06:27.909 --> 06:28.743
‎"Patient"?

120
06:29.827 --> 06:32.413
‎What kind of patient sleeps like this?

121
06:32.496 --> 06:35.374
‎Anyone lying in an ER bed is my patient.

122
06:35.458 --> 06:37.001
‎And there are other patients too.

123
06:37.835 --> 06:39.212
‎She stopped at an accident scene,

124
06:39.295 --> 06:41.297
‎helped with the rescue, ‎and even donated blood.

125
06:41.881 --> 06:43.507
‎Dr. Gye is insanely cool, isn't she?

126
06:43.591 --> 06:45.927
‎And I'm the one who's insanely exhausted.

127
06:46.010 --> 06:47.303
‎Seriously, what on earth…

128
06:47.386 --> 06:51.515
‎She fulfilled her duty as a doctor, ‎so I don't get why no one is praising her.

129
06:51.599 --> 06:54.644
‎I'll just leave that thought ‎and head to the OR.

130
06:58.689 --> 07:00.691
‎Well, duty equals money to her.

131
07:00.775 --> 07:03.194
‎How much will she charge this time?

132
07:15.790 --> 07:17.208
‎Has the accident been sorted out?

133
07:17.291 --> 07:19.794
‎Yes. Luckily, there were no fatalities.

134
07:20.294 --> 07:22.380
‎Other than the patient ‎who needed a transfusion,

135
07:22.463 --> 07:24.131
‎no one else was seriously injured.

136
07:25.466 --> 07:26.300
‎Good work.

137
07:26.384 --> 07:28.844
‎Director Bu, it's time for the conference.

138
07:29.345 --> 07:30.388
‎You're leaving?

139
07:30.930 --> 07:31.889
‎Just like that?

140
07:33.140 --> 07:36.060
‎So you only came here ‎to check on a member of your staff.

141
07:37.603 --> 07:38.729
‎Hey, come on.

142
07:38.813 --> 07:41.983
‎It's been a million years ‎since any of you came down to the ER.

143
07:42.066 --> 07:44.443
‎The new director ‎graced us with his presence,

144
07:44.527 --> 07:46.487
‎so I was genuinely touched.

145
07:46.571 --> 07:49.490
‎I had high hopes, ‎and you're just taking off?

146
07:49.574 --> 07:51.409
‎That sounds a lot like sarcasm.

147
07:51.492 --> 07:53.327
‎Sorry, I haven't slept in two days.

148
07:53.411 --> 07:55.288
‎And yes, that was sarcasm.

149
07:55.371 --> 07:58.833
‎You're not the only one. ‎I barely made it home last night myself.

150
07:58.916 --> 08:01.043
‎Most cases should be handled here.

151
08:01.127 --> 08:03.337
‎That's what emergency medicine is for.

152
08:03.421 --> 08:04.380
‎I see.

153
08:05.089 --> 08:09.635
‎The sole reason emergency medicine exists ‎is to handle most cases, is it?

154
08:09.719 --> 08:11.679
‎Is that why nobody was around that day?

155
08:11.762 --> 08:14.265
‎-What are you talking about? ‎-That's what you're saying.

156
08:14.849 --> 08:17.768
‎That we didn't handle things better, ‎and that's why Mr. Seo…

157
08:17.852 --> 08:18.686
‎That's enough.

158
08:24.567 --> 08:27.737
‎-Let's handle the ER's request right now. ‎-Yes, sir.

159
08:31.490 --> 08:33.701
‎Hospitals are always short-staffed.

160
08:34.869 --> 08:38.706
‎For now, ‎I temporarily assigned a new doctor here.

161
08:40.291 --> 08:42.001
‎What? Just like that?

162
08:42.501 --> 08:43.794
‎When are they starting?

163
08:45.171 --> 08:46.631
‎They're already here.

164
08:46.714 --> 08:47.590
‎What?

165
08:51.260 --> 08:52.345
‎You mean that snorer…

166
09:00.269 --> 09:02.271
‎Hey. You're staying with her.

167
09:07.777 --> 09:08.694
‎Who are you again?

168
09:08.778 --> 09:10.029
‎I'm an intern.

169
09:10.529 --> 09:13.658
‎I've just been assigned to Dr. Gye.

170
09:14.325 --> 09:15.159
‎The two of you?

171
09:17.370 --> 09:20.247
‎At around 8:20 a.m. this morning ‎in Seonam, Gyeonggi Province…

172
09:20.331 --> 09:21.415
‎That must be it.

173
09:21.499 --> 09:24.835
‎…a school bus carrying students ‎collided with a box truck.

174
09:24.919 --> 09:26.045
‎There were no fatalities,

175
09:26.128 --> 09:29.090
‎but five people were seriously injured, ‎and many others sustained minor injuries.

176
09:29.173 --> 09:31.676
‎Su-jeong won't get in trouble, will she?

177
09:31.759 --> 09:33.344
‎Surely not.

178
09:34.303 --> 09:35.930
‎-She did her duty as a doctor. ‎-‎In other news,

179
09:36.013 --> 09:38.683
‎the first anniversary is approaching ‎for the late Seo Jin-yeong,

180
09:38.766 --> 09:42.228
‎an EMT with emergency medicine ‎at Guseo University ‎Seonam ‎Medical ‎Center.

181
09:42.311 --> 09:46.107
‎Mr. Seo's family had filed a lawsuit ‎to hold the hospital accountable,

182
09:46.190 --> 09:48.567
‎and the court delivered its verdict today.

183
09:48.651 --> 09:52.238
‎The court ruled in favor of GUMC ‎in the first trial.

184
09:53.072 --> 09:56.325
‎The court emphasized that the hospital ‎made every effort to save Mr. Seo,

185
09:56.409 --> 09:59.161
‎and while the bereaved ‎might have perceived

186
09:59.245 --> 10:01.080
‎some shortcomings in the process,

187
10:01.163 --> 10:04.166
‎those issues were due to ‎Mr. Seo's medical condition

188
10:04.250 --> 10:07.294
‎rather than any failure ‎in the hospital's response.

189
10:08.879 --> 10:10.297
‎Director.

190
10:10.381 --> 10:12.508
‎We won. Isn't that enough?

191
10:13.092 --> 10:15.177
‎His family filed an appeal.

192
10:15.261 --> 10:16.345
‎Of course, they did.

193
10:16.429 --> 10:19.515
‎Granted, this happened ‎while Director Kim was in charge,

194
10:19.598 --> 10:23.602
‎but public sentiment is actually worse ‎now that we've won.

195
10:23.686 --> 10:25.187
‎We need to find a way--

196
10:27.565 --> 10:28.733
‎Excuse me.

197
10:32.611 --> 10:34.947
‎-I didn't have time to throw anything out. ‎-I see.

198
10:35.030 --> 10:35.865
‎Wait.

199
10:36.949 --> 10:38.409
‎Oh goodness.

200
10:38.492 --> 10:40.202
‎Thank you.

201
10:41.871 --> 10:45.750
‎On top of this, everyone's constantly away ‎on business trips and seminars,

202
10:45.833 --> 10:48.586
‎and the med school quota issue ‎is coming up again.

203
10:49.295 --> 10:50.796
‎If people go on strike again,

204
10:50.880 --> 10:53.340
‎I'll be the first one to do it.

205
10:54.216 --> 10:57.303
‎Doctors complain about staff shortages, ‎yet they're never available…

206
10:57.386 --> 11:00.055
‎That's why we can't fire Dr. Gye.

207
11:00.139 --> 11:00.973
‎So just stop.

208
11:02.224 --> 11:03.934
‎Where did you even find someone like her?

209
11:12.401 --> 11:14.528
‎The hospital's been ‎in an uproar these days

210
11:14.612 --> 11:15.529
‎because of her?

211
11:16.197 --> 11:17.031
‎Dr. Kim.

212
11:17.114 --> 11:20.493
‎Dr. Gye isn't a pain in the neck ‎like the rumors say.

213
11:21.076 --> 11:22.536
‎Is she my superior or my subordinate?

214
11:22.620 --> 11:24.705
‎What? I'm not quite sure…

215
11:26.040 --> 11:27.291
‎Fine, then answer this.

216
11:27.374 --> 11:29.710
‎Do I need to wait on her or teach her?

217
11:29.793 --> 11:33.047
‎I haven't been around her long, ‎but I know one thing.

218
11:33.130 --> 11:34.507
‎You'll need to do both.

219
11:34.590 --> 11:35.966
‎Both? Then she's a pain in the neck.

220
11:36.050 --> 11:37.343
‎I'm hungry.

221
11:38.052 --> 11:38.886
‎Dr. Gye, are you okay?

222
11:38.969 --> 11:40.888
‎I brought your white coat.

223
11:40.971 --> 11:42.556
‎How long have you been awake?

224
11:42.640 --> 11:44.433
‎-A while. ‎-Since when?

225
11:46.185 --> 11:47.811
‎"What? Is he a doctor too?"

226
11:48.812 --> 11:51.357
‎"He's an intern, ‎despite looking like a clueless fool."

227
11:51.440 --> 11:52.858
‎You've been awake for some time.

228
11:52.942 --> 11:55.277
‎-Wait, was that about me? ‎-Why didn't you get up?

229
11:55.361 --> 11:57.238
‎-Do I look like a clueless fool? ‎-Too bothersome.

230
11:57.321 --> 11:58.405
‎What was bothersome?

231
11:58.489 --> 12:00.491
‎The clueless fool, the rage-smile,

232
12:01.200 --> 12:02.159
‎and the suck-ups in surgery.

233
12:02.243 --> 12:04.745
‎Dr. Jo is "rage-smile"? Awesome.

234
12:04.828 --> 12:07.039
‎Can you tell me ‎where your next rotation is?

235
12:07.122 --> 12:08.249
‎Why, sir?

236
12:10.292 --> 12:12.294
‎I'm not sure about emergency medicine…

237
12:12.378 --> 12:14.922
‎Thanks so much. ‎Good choice. Great. Excellent.

238
12:15.714 --> 12:17.841
‎You can wake someone who's sleeping,

239
12:17.925 --> 12:20.219
‎but not someone pretending to be asleep.

240
12:20.803 --> 12:23.430
‎It's even harder to teach someone ‎who pretends to know everything.

241
12:24.974 --> 12:28.561
‎You'd be better off with someone like him ‎who doesn't know anything.

242
12:29.186 --> 12:31.730
‎She's basically passing you off.

243
12:31.814 --> 12:33.857
‎I didn't see it at first, ‎but now she seems like…

244
12:33.941 --> 12:35.109
‎A nutjob, right?

245
12:35.192 --> 12:37.486
‎You have a knack for whispering ‎so everyone can hear.

246
12:38.487 --> 12:40.322
‎It's a good technique. ‎Excellent for raising low BP.

247
12:40.406 --> 12:41.907
‎Really? I'll have to try it out.

248
12:43.033 --> 12:44.034
‎From what I heard earlier,

249
12:44.577 --> 12:48.330
‎you're the one with high blood pressure, ‎raising your voice like that.

250
12:51.166 --> 12:52.126
‎I'm Kim Seong-jin.

251
12:52.209 --> 12:53.544
‎I'm Gye Su-jeong.

252
12:54.753 --> 12:55.629
‎I'm Park Tae-gyeong.

253
13:00.092 --> 13:02.177
‎…those issues were due to ‎Mr. Seo's medical condition

254
13:02.261 --> 13:04.221
‎-rather than any failure‎… ‎-Hello, sir.

255
13:04.305 --> 13:05.347
‎-Hello. ‎-Hello.

256
13:06.765 --> 13:08.976
‎Hey, it's fine. Just watch it.

257
13:09.059 --> 13:11.270
‎There's no need to be secretive about it.

258
13:11.854 --> 13:13.731
‎All that testifying and questioning…

259
13:13.814 --> 13:16.900
‎It's been tough, ‎but we made it past the hardest part.

260
13:16.984 --> 13:19.111
‎It might not be over yet ‎since they're appealing.

261
13:19.612 --> 13:21.989
‎By the way, ‎Dr. Kim Seong-jin is the same as ever.

262
13:22.072 --> 13:23.782
‎What if he testifies in their favor?

263
13:23.866 --> 13:25.200
‎There's nothing for him to say.

264
13:25.909 --> 13:27.036
‎Which is probably why

265
13:27.119 --> 13:31.498
‎Dr. Kim feels so bothered by it.

266
13:34.209 --> 13:36.670
‎-Why won't you check your messages? ‎-What?

267
13:37.880 --> 13:39.173
‎This won't work.

268
13:39.256 --> 13:40.716
‎I can't open an OR in their condition.

269
13:40.799 --> 13:42.593
‎Why not? I need to operate right now.

270
13:42.676 --> 13:44.970
‎No. We need to evaluate them more.

271
13:45.679 --> 13:46.764
‎-Hello. ‎-Hey.

272
13:46.847 --> 13:49.350
‎I'm sorry about earlier.

273
13:50.100 --> 13:51.727
‎And thank you for calling me.

274
13:52.811 --> 13:53.646
‎Why are you by yourself?

275
13:53.729 --> 13:56.148
‎Dr. Gye is working in the ER now.

276
13:56.231 --> 13:58.150
‎What? Why?

277
14:01.236 --> 14:02.821
‎Is staffing a joke to you?

278
14:02.905 --> 14:04.114
‎What are you doing?

279
14:04.198 --> 14:07.451
‎The director assigned her there ‎because they're short-staffed.

280
14:07.534 --> 14:09.995
‎How does having a talent like that there ‎help general surgery?

281
14:10.079 --> 14:11.997
‎All right, precious intern.

282
14:12.081 --> 14:13.707
‎You came to get your things, right?

283
14:14.291 --> 14:16.669
‎Let's go. Have a nice day.

284
14:20.589 --> 14:22.966
‎Even kids don't bully like this. ‎What's wrong with you?

285
14:23.050 --> 14:24.843
‎Hey, it's none of your business.

286
14:24.927 --> 14:26.220
‎Just give me an OR already.

287
14:26.303 --> 14:28.430
‎Who'll take the blame ‎if the patient dies in surgery?

288
14:28.514 --> 14:31.350
‎You know I don't allow ‎high-risk surgeries.

289
14:31.433 --> 14:32.434
‎Find someone else.

290
14:33.519 --> 14:34.895
‎Someone else? Like who?

291
14:39.358 --> 14:41.819
‎I'm busy, but to help ‎the future of Korean medicine,

292
14:41.902 --> 14:43.112
‎I'll give you two minutes.

293
14:44.196 --> 14:46.865
‎Dr. Kim mentioned Mr. Seo earlier.

294
14:46.949 --> 14:50.786
‎Is that the person on the news who died ‎from an SAH last year during his shift?

295
14:50.869 --> 14:51.829
‎Yeah. What else?

296
14:51.912 --> 14:55.207
‎Did he really die because there was ‎nobody available to perform a craniotomy?

297
14:55.290 --> 14:57.292
‎Yeah, but you're only half right.

298
14:58.669 --> 15:01.130
‎Then were Dr. Kim or Dr. Bae,

299
15:01.213 --> 15:03.340
‎-who performed the endovascular coiling-- ‎-No.

300
15:03.424 --> 15:05.718
‎ENDOVASCULAR COILING: A TREATMENT ‎THAT DOESN'T REQUIRE CRANIOTOMY

301
15:05.801 --> 15:07.761
‎They did everything they could.

302
15:09.221 --> 15:11.265
‎Dr. Kim wasn't even on shift that day.

303
15:12.725 --> 15:14.309
‎He was up all night and was heading home

304
15:14.393 --> 15:16.895
‎-when he saw Mr. Seo passed out. ‎-Mr. Seo?

305
15:16.979 --> 15:18.731
‎He was slumped over the ER desk,

306
15:18.814 --> 15:21.066
‎-so everyone thought he had fallen asleep. ‎-Mr. Seo?

307
15:21.150 --> 15:23.736
‎Things had been hectic ‎because ‎of ‎a major car accident that night.

308
15:24.403 --> 15:25.821
‎Help! Over here!

309
15:26.989 --> 15:28.824
‎Mr. Seo!

310
15:28.907 --> 15:29.742
‎Mr. Seo!

311
15:35.706 --> 15:36.874
‎Dr. Bae.

312
15:36.957 --> 15:40.377
‎Are we just going to ‎let Mr. Seo go like this?

313
15:40.961 --> 15:43.047
‎We have ten neurosurgeons,

314
15:43.130 --> 15:44.423
‎but no one to clip an aneurysm?

315
15:44.506 --> 15:46.925
‎His intracranial pressure is too high.

316
15:47.009 --> 15:49.428
‎We should do a craniotomy and clip it,

317
15:49.511 --> 15:51.388
‎-but it's already-- ‎-Then page someone.

318
15:51.472 --> 15:53.015
‎Neither of them is here.

319
15:53.098 --> 15:54.349
‎Are you serious? Neither one?

320
15:56.518 --> 15:58.562
‎Forget it. Dr. Bae…

321
15:59.063 --> 16:00.773
‎Let's try coiling first.

322
16:00.856 --> 16:03.400
‎We have no time to lose. ‎I'll work on getting him transferred.

323
16:03.484 --> 16:05.319
‎-Look… ‎-Hey, Bae Heung-gon!

324
16:07.112 --> 16:09.239
‎Please, I'm begging you.

325
16:09.990 --> 16:11.742
‎Mr. Seo has worked here for ten years.

326
16:11.825 --> 16:15.162
‎The hospital he works for ‎should at least try something to save him.

327
16:16.538 --> 16:18.957
‎It's only proper, ‎and it's the right thing to do.

328
16:19.041 --> 16:20.375
‎ANGIOGRAPHY SUITE 3

329
16:22.586 --> 16:24.296
‎I can't get to it.

330
16:24.963 --> 16:26.340
‎Endovascular coiling won't work.

331
16:26.423 --> 16:29.510
‎-Then let's call the attendings again-- ‎-One's in Germany for training.

332
16:29.593 --> 16:31.887
‎The other is in Naju ‎for his mother-in-law's funeral.

333
16:31.970 --> 16:33.305
‎Then I'll get him transferred.

334
16:33.388 --> 16:35.724
‎Dr. Nam at Junggyeong University Hospital ‎said they'd take him.

335
16:35.808 --> 16:38.560
‎I said it's no use. His ICP is too high.

336
16:38.644 --> 16:41.480
‎He was finally transferred, ‎but the patient died.

337
16:42.898 --> 16:45.859
‎His ICP was too high, ‎so even if we'd operated on him here,

338
16:45.943 --> 16:47.945
‎there was a low chance of success.

339
16:48.028 --> 16:50.114
‎That's what you got wrong, ‎and it's the crux of the lawsuit.

340
16:50.197 --> 16:51.198
‎I'm heading in.

341
16:52.157 --> 16:53.784
‎You said there was ‎a low chance of success.

342
16:55.244 --> 17:00.124
‎Are you saying he was meant to die ‎no matter what?

343
17:01.375 --> 17:03.418
‎A doctor shouldn't say that.

344
17:04.128 --> 17:05.212
‎Then what should one say?

345
17:05.796 --> 17:07.422
‎"I couldn't save him. I'll go to jail."

346
17:07.506 --> 17:09.383
‎Or maybe "I'm sorry"?

347
17:10.425 --> 17:12.052
‎Doctors are human too. We have limits.

348
17:12.136 --> 17:14.805
‎But if there'd been one more doctor ‎who could do a craniotomy,

349
17:14.888 --> 17:16.348
‎they could've gone all in and--

350
17:16.431 --> 17:17.808
‎What are you, Hippocrates?

351
17:19.017 --> 17:21.895
‎Nobody's impressed ‎by an aneurysm clipping anymore.

352
17:22.729 --> 17:25.190
‎Spending four hours ‎looking through a tiny microscope

353
17:25.274 --> 17:27.693
‎and digging around a bloody brain?

354
17:27.776 --> 17:30.279
‎Fine, let's say we pushed through ‎and pulled off the surgery.

355
17:30.362 --> 17:31.530
‎You know what sucks?

356
17:32.114 --> 17:33.574
‎The clip could slip at any second.

357
17:34.199 --> 17:35.909
‎Who'd take the blame ‎if the aneurysm ruptured

358
17:35.993 --> 17:37.619
‎and killed or disabled ‎the patient for life?

359
17:38.745 --> 17:41.165
‎Do you know how many malpractice suits ‎come with this surgery?

360
17:41.248 --> 17:42.583
‎And clipping costs a fortune.

361
17:43.208 --> 17:46.211
‎It's a major six-person team surgery, ‎but reimbursement rates are trash.

362
17:46.295 --> 17:47.254
‎Listen.

363
17:48.630 --> 17:50.841
‎Spare me the lecture on ‎what doctors can or can't say,

364
17:51.925 --> 17:53.093
‎and learn craniotomy yourself.

365
17:53.677 --> 17:54.553
‎You do it.

366
17:55.512 --> 17:57.890
‎I'm going to learn coiling from Dr. Bae,

367
17:57.973 --> 18:01.268
‎a non-surgical procedure with lower risk, ‎fewer staff, and better money.

368
18:01.351 --> 18:02.603
‎That's it for me.

369
18:03.645 --> 18:04.897
‎I'll only work within my limits.

370
18:06.356 --> 18:08.817
‎So does saying this mean

371
18:09.943 --> 18:10.986
‎I'm not a real doctor?

372
18:11.069 --> 18:11.987
‎Huh?

373
18:13.071 --> 18:13.906
‎Answer me.

374
18:17.868 --> 18:19.828
‎If you hit people like this,

375
18:20.662 --> 18:22.331
‎they could end up dead ‎or disabled for life.

376
18:22.414 --> 18:24.750
‎That's what Eung-gu said.

377
18:27.377 --> 18:29.296
‎When a cerebral aneurysm occurs,

378
18:29.379 --> 18:31.006
‎one-third of patients die instantly.

379
18:31.590 --> 18:33.091
‎Another third die en route.

380
18:33.759 --> 18:35.761
‎Only the remaining third

381
18:36.345 --> 18:38.138
‎make it to the hospital alive.

382
18:39.306 --> 18:41.642
‎Mr. Seo beat the one-third odds ‎of instant death

383
18:41.725 --> 18:44.603
‎and was lucky enough ‎to be in the hospital.

384
18:45.938 --> 18:47.564
‎Are you ignoring these odds?

385
18:47.648 --> 18:51.193
‎Maybe you're okay operating on those odds ‎and letting a patient die--

386
18:51.276 --> 18:53.028
‎Dr. Ma, what are you doing?

387
18:53.111 --> 18:54.196
‎Get inside and prep.

388
18:54.988 --> 18:57.824
‎Aren't you supposed to get ‎double board-certified like Dr. Bae?

389
18:57.908 --> 18:59.660
‎You won't survive ‎a second residency like this.

390
19:00.953 --> 19:02.371
‎Given your current skills…

391
19:03.121 --> 19:05.082
‎you'll see a pile of lawsuits ‎even if you play it safe.

392
19:05.165 --> 19:07.834
‎Get in there and learn, resident.

393
19:07.918 --> 19:09.336
‎Go inside.

394
19:18.553 --> 19:19.888
‎Dr. Gye.

395
19:20.889 --> 19:23.809
‎It feels like I'm putting out fires ‎you've been starting.

396
19:23.892 --> 19:24.893
‎It's my imagination, right?

397
19:24.977 --> 19:26.520
‎No, it's the truth.

398
19:27.688 --> 19:29.356
‎Also, I didn't start this fire.

399
19:30.190 --> 19:32.192
‎I'm the one who started it.

400
19:32.276 --> 19:34.194
‎I crossed the line with Dr. Ma.

401
19:35.153 --> 19:35.988
‎I'm sorry.

402
19:36.071 --> 19:40.117
‎Don't provoke anyone entering my OR ‎30 minutes before surgery.

403
19:40.659 --> 19:41.952
‎It'll distract them.

404
19:42.744 --> 19:44.746
‎We're 31 minutes and 20 seconds away.

405
19:46.331 --> 19:48.375
‎Dr. Gye, please stop.

406
19:49.543 --> 19:51.545
‎You two are a chaotic duo.

407
19:57.050 --> 19:59.678
‎You can't even observe the surgery ‎because of me.

408
20:01.388 --> 20:02.889
‎It's not your fault.

409
20:02.973 --> 20:04.766
‎I'm waiting for a surprise visit.

410
20:04.850 --> 20:07.185
‎You get surprise visits?

411
20:07.853 --> 20:08.770
‎That's unexpected.

412
20:10.439 --> 20:11.606
‎Oh, here.

413
20:12.482 --> 20:13.984
‎You usually get these ‎when you donate blood.

414
20:15.485 --> 20:16.528
‎I wish I could do it every day.

415
20:17.738 --> 20:19.281
‎Don't you dare do it every day!

416
20:19.364 --> 20:21.366
‎I'll draw your blood and spinal fluid too!

417
20:21.450 --> 20:23.076
‎What are you doing? Who are you?

418
20:24.286 --> 20:25.662
‎Ms. Jang.

419
20:25.746 --> 20:26.872
‎Ms. Jang?

420
20:26.955 --> 20:28.040
‎The lady you live with?

421
20:28.123 --> 20:30.000
‎The one who uses you for free labor?

422
20:31.543 --> 20:35.422
‎I'm tired from giving blood ‎and working today.

423
20:35.505 --> 20:36.923
‎Make me a good meal at home.

424
20:37.007 --> 20:40.385
‎Things would've gone fine without you. ‎Why get in the way?

425
20:40.886 --> 20:42.387
‎I said keep to yourself for a bit.

426
20:42.471 --> 20:44.389
‎Dr. Gye was amazing today.

427
20:44.473 --> 20:45.849
‎She shouldn't be amazing!

428
20:47.851 --> 20:51.980
‎You need to focus on doing big cases ‎and making a lot of money.

429
20:52.064 --> 20:54.900
‎Besides, why are you working in the ER?

430
20:54.983 --> 20:57.027
‎You can't operate now, ‎and you won't make money.

431
20:57.819 --> 20:59.988
‎Just keep to yourself ‎until you get back to general surgery…

432
21:00.572 --> 21:01.698
‎Oh my goodness.

433
21:02.532 --> 21:03.492
‎Good heavens.

434
21:03.575 --> 21:05.243
‎I can't believe ‎I spoke like that in front of you.

435
21:05.327 --> 21:07.704
‎-I'm sorry, Doctor. ‎-It's okay.

436
21:08.413 --> 21:10.123
‎I'm an intern. My name is Park Tae-gyeong.

437
21:10.207 --> 21:11.500
‎I see.

438
21:12.167 --> 21:13.627
‎Hello.

439
21:13.710 --> 21:16.463
‎I'm the head of the country's ‎first-ever locum tenens agency.

440
21:16.546 --> 21:18.048
‎My name is Jang Hui-suk.

441
21:18.673 --> 21:22.052
‎You could say ‎I'm Dr. Gye Su-jeong's agent.

442
21:22.636 --> 21:24.471
‎Oh, you might become

443
21:25.055 --> 21:27.349
‎one of our future clients ‎or locums in the future,

444
21:27.933 --> 21:29.309
‎so please take this, sir.

445
21:29.393 --> 21:30.435
‎DIRECTOR JANG HUI-SUK

446
21:30.519 --> 21:32.646
‎Oh, you don't have to call me "sir."

447
21:32.729 --> 21:35.107
‎Of course, I do.

448
21:35.190 --> 21:37.317
‎You're pursuing a demanding path of study.

449
21:38.402 --> 21:40.404
‎Goodness, I'm getting thirsty.

450
21:40.904 --> 21:43.615
‎Go get something for me and Dr. Park.

451
21:43.698 --> 21:46.827
‎-I'll go, ma'am. ‎-No, no. Please sit down.

452
21:46.910 --> 21:47.786
‎Go on.

453
21:48.537 --> 21:50.872
‎I can tell by looking at you

454
21:50.956 --> 21:53.333
‎that there are ‎other doctors in your family.

455
21:53.417 --> 21:54.501
‎How did you know that?

456
22:00.674 --> 22:01.508
‎Ma'am?

457
22:02.676 --> 22:03.510
‎Ma'am?

458
22:04.386 --> 22:05.220
‎Me?

459
22:05.303 --> 22:08.432
‎Yes. Can I borrow some tissue from you?

460
22:09.683 --> 22:13.728
‎Wiping something sticky with tissue ‎will make a big mess.

461
22:13.812 --> 22:14.646
‎Use this instead.

462
22:16.064 --> 22:17.190
‎Here, take it.

463
22:21.236 --> 22:22.863
‎It really works better. Thank you.

464
22:24.156 --> 22:26.533
‎I haven't seen you before. ‎Which department do you work in?

465
22:29.786 --> 22:31.371
‎I go here and there.

466
22:31.872 --> 22:33.748
‎I do something like contract work.

467
22:33.832 --> 22:35.876
‎I do contract work too. Contract cleaning.

468
22:35.959 --> 22:37.210
‎I go here and there too.

469
22:38.670 --> 22:39.504
‎You're my senior then.

470
22:39.588 --> 22:41.214
‎Goodness, your senior?

471
22:41.298 --> 22:42.257
‎Excuse me then.

472
22:46.386 --> 22:47.220
‎Are you okay?

473
22:47.846 --> 22:49.431
‎Oh, I'm okay.

474
22:50.056 --> 22:51.266
‎Have you felt this pain before?

475
22:51.349 --> 22:55.729
‎Something new hurts every day, you know.

476
22:57.355 --> 22:58.231
‎It's okay.

477
23:02.444 --> 23:04.863
‎Thank you. I appreciate it.

478
23:11.494 --> 23:13.496
‎I think a part of Dr. Kim feels like

479
23:13.580 --> 23:16.333
‎he's responsible for what happened.

480
23:16.917 --> 23:18.793
‎There was a huge uproar

481
23:18.877 --> 23:23.256
‎when CCTV footage was released, ‎showing Mr. Seo slumped in the ER alone.

482
23:23.340 --> 23:24.299
‎I saw it too.

483
23:24.382 --> 23:27.636
‎It made me think that ‎even if I collapsed in a hospital,

484
23:27.719 --> 23:29.554
‎no one would know.

485
23:29.638 --> 23:30.889
‎In a hospital, of all places.

486
23:30.972 --> 23:33.558
‎-That's why people were so upset. ‎-Right.

487
23:33.642 --> 23:36.686
‎But how did that get leaked to the public?

488
23:37.437 --> 23:38.897
‎Someone posted on the message board.

489
23:38.980 --> 23:39.981
‎Goodness.

490
23:40.065 --> 23:42.150
‎So they tried to ‎hunt down the whistleblower

491
23:42.234 --> 23:46.780
‎by calling in all the EMTs and nurses ‎and questioning them.

492
23:46.863 --> 23:48.490
‎Everyone but the doctors, right?

493
23:48.573 --> 23:50.158
‎They never found the person,

494
23:50.242 --> 23:53.203
‎but apparently the Korean Health ‎and Medical Workers' Union even protested.

495
23:53.286 --> 23:55.247
‎Must have been traumatic ‎for the hospital, right?

496
23:56.790 --> 24:00.377
‎Oh my. I just used a medical term ‎in front of a doctor.

497
24:04.881 --> 24:05.840
‎What are you doing?

498
24:06.716 --> 24:08.260
‎Are you drinking that or not?

499
24:08.969 --> 24:12.264
‎This young gentleman's parent turned ‎their plastic surgery clinic in Busan

500
24:12.347 --> 24:14.140
‎into a regional hub hospital.

501
24:14.224 --> 24:15.642
‎Pay attention to the great doctor's son.

502
24:16.601 --> 24:18.520
‎She couldn't get it on the first try.

503
24:19.396 --> 24:20.689
‎Not the can or the wet wipe.

504
24:25.902 --> 24:28.321
‎I like this time of day.

505
24:28.405 --> 24:31.116
‎Everyone quietly writes up ‎what happened during work,

506
24:31.199 --> 24:33.743
‎gives each other notice, ‎and gets ready to leave.

507
24:34.244 --> 24:36.288
‎-Who's leaving? ‎-This doctor here.

508
24:38.623 --> 24:40.417
‎If you have any questions, ask her now.

509
24:40.500 --> 24:41.626
‎It's almost time.

510
24:44.379 --> 24:46.589
‎So, how did you know

511
24:46.673 --> 24:49.009
‎it was acid reflux and not chest pain?

512
24:50.010 --> 24:51.970
‎Ms. Ha Mi-ju, 61 years old.

513
24:52.053 --> 24:55.056
‎She's complaining of extreme chest pain,

514
24:55.140 --> 24:57.517
‎but her test results came back fine.

515
24:57.600 --> 25:00.186
‎You came in with the same symptoms ‎at dawn the other day.

516
25:00.270 --> 25:03.315
‎The pain woke her up at night. ‎It's especially bad at night.

517
25:03.398 --> 25:07.110
‎Okay. Let me listen to your chest again.

518
25:07.193 --> 25:08.111
‎Ms. Ha?

519
25:08.695 --> 25:10.196
‎Did you eat before coming here?

520
25:10.947 --> 25:12.073
‎No.

521
25:14.701 --> 25:15.785
‎Then Ms. Ha,

522
25:15.869 --> 25:19.372
‎do you usually drink a lot of coffee ‎or eat greasy food?

523
25:19.456 --> 25:20.373
‎Yes.

524
25:20.457 --> 25:22.625
‎Let me apply pressure to your abdomen.

525
25:23.501 --> 25:25.295
‎-Does that hurt? ‎-Yes, it does.

526
25:27.213 --> 25:29.174
‎I could tell ‎from ‎her ‎awkward ‎hand ‎placement

527
25:29.257 --> 25:31.676
‎and the radius of her hand gesture ‎when signaling pain.

528
25:33.261 --> 25:34.304
‎What a cool description.

529
25:34.387 --> 25:35.847
‎Can I write that in the report?

530
25:35.930 --> 25:37.098
‎What do you think?

531
25:37.766 --> 25:40.018
‎I spent a long time somewhere ‎I didn't know the language well,

532
25:40.101 --> 25:43.313
‎so I had to focus on behavior and attitude ‎during examinations.

533
25:44.564 --> 25:47.150
‎Why do you think ‎Ms. Ha described her symptoms wrong?

534
25:47.233 --> 25:49.944
‎It happens. That's why doctors ‎need to ask the right questions.

535
25:51.154 --> 25:52.489
‎I missed a lot of signs

536
25:52.572 --> 25:55.075
‎because my mind was ‎all over the place today.

537
25:56.659 --> 25:59.162
‎Not many people are good at describing…

538
26:00.747 --> 26:01.664
‎their own pain.

539
26:03.875 --> 26:04.918
‎I suppose so.

540
26:06.503 --> 26:10.548
‎After watching people fight over consults ‎and get mad about criticism,

541
26:11.424 --> 26:14.177
‎I'm not sure what to make of ‎this heartwarming scene.

542
26:15.053 --> 26:17.180
‎On that note, ‎let's order a late-night snack…

543
26:17.847 --> 26:18.723
‎Goodbye.

544
26:19.599 --> 26:21.393
‎Wait, you're really clocking out?

545
26:21.476 --> 26:23.686
‎Dr. Park, did she just go home?

546
26:23.770 --> 26:24.604
‎Yes.

547
26:41.329 --> 26:42.372
‎Get it together.

548
26:50.171 --> 26:51.047
‎It's gone cold.

549
26:55.718 --> 26:57.011
‎Dr. Gye, are you okay?

550
26:57.095 --> 26:58.596
‎I brought your white coat.

551
26:58.680 --> 27:00.140
‎How long have you been awake?

552
27:00.223 --> 27:02.809
‎GYE SU-JEONG

553
27:02.892 --> 27:04.394
‎It looked smudged.

554
27:08.773 --> 27:10.066
‎I'll make her a new one.

555
27:18.366 --> 27:20.410
‎GYE SU-JEONG

556
27:26.040 --> 27:28.293
‎Based on what I've seen so far,

557
27:29.711 --> 27:32.464
‎it'll be a while before Dr. Gye ‎gets a proper white coat.

558
27:36.384 --> 27:38.636
‎I'll have to make some more.

559
27:54.152 --> 27:56.779
‎(UNKNOWN)

560
28:02.577 --> 28:04.162
‎You skipped a meal again, right?

561
28:06.664 --> 28:07.499
‎Thank you.

562
28:09.209 --> 28:13.338
‎I heard the paramedics ‎talk among themselves

563
28:13.922 --> 28:16.508
‎that the GUMC ER in Gyeonggi Province ‎accepts all patients.

564
28:17.467 --> 28:19.844
‎That there's a good doctor working here.

565
28:20.845 --> 28:23.890
‎So stop getting angry ‎and threatening to quit.

566
28:23.973 --> 28:25.225
‎Just hang in there.

567
28:26.809 --> 28:29.479
‎I want my kid to visit me at work, ‎meet a good doctor like you,

568
28:30.063 --> 28:31.606
‎and decide she wants to become one.

569
28:36.819 --> 28:37.946
‎Eat before the noodles get soggy.

570
28:48.331 --> 28:49.916
‎Hello, ma'am.

571
28:50.792 --> 28:53.628
‎I work at the same hospital ‎as Mr. Seo Jin-yeong…

572
29:09.477 --> 29:11.312
‎GUSEO UNIVERSITY SEONAM MEDICAL CENTER

573
29:11.396 --> 29:13.690
‎We're seeing the same thing, right?

574
29:13.773 --> 29:14.607
‎Yes.

575
29:14.691 --> 29:17.944
‎It's the same sight we saw yesterday.

576
29:22.282 --> 29:23.867
‎Dr. Gye.

577
29:25.118 --> 29:26.286
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong.

578
29:26.369 --> 29:29.539
‎Are you pretending to be asleep, ‎or am I unable to wake you?

579
29:30.039 --> 29:32.083
‎I think she's really asleep.

580
29:32.166 --> 29:34.210
‎Why sleep here ‎and not in the on-call room?

581
29:34.294 --> 29:36.087
‎And didn't she leave work ‎on the dot yesterday?

582
29:38.548 --> 29:40.008
‎Dr. Gye.

583
29:40.508 --> 29:41.342
‎Dr. Gye!

584
29:42.427 --> 29:43.261
‎Did you sleep well?

585
29:48.683 --> 29:51.936
‎These uncomfortable hospital beds ‎are somehow great for deep sleep.

586
29:53.104 --> 29:54.480
‎Are you kidding me?

587
29:54.564 --> 29:56.024
‎Do we need empty beds right now?

588
29:56.107 --> 30:00.570
‎This is where patients get treated ‎or wait to get treated, okay?

589
30:00.653 --> 30:02.530
‎You're lucky we don't have ‎an incoming rush--

590
30:02.614 --> 30:03.656
‎So there's no rush of patients.

591
30:04.449 --> 30:07.118
‎Didn't you go home yesterday?

592
30:07.201 --> 30:08.369
‎I went home and came in early.

593
30:16.294 --> 30:17.420
‎Are you looking for someone?

594
30:18.630 --> 30:20.590
‎The morning shift hasn't started yet.

595
30:21.883 --> 30:23.009
‎In that case…

596
30:24.844 --> 30:25.678
‎"In that case"?

597
30:26.346 --> 30:27.180
‎Huh?

598
30:37.440 --> 30:38.358
‎Hello, Dr. Jo.

599
30:38.942 --> 30:40.234
‎Pulled an all-nighter?

600
30:40.318 --> 30:41.194
‎Pick something.

601
30:41.277 --> 30:43.321
‎It's okay. I'm fine.

602
30:48.618 --> 30:49.744
‎Are you picking up groceries?

603
31:01.089 --> 31:02.048
‎Now I'm awake.

604
31:04.592 --> 31:06.219
‎Did you talk to Dr. Ma?

605
31:07.428 --> 31:08.596
‎No.

606
31:08.680 --> 31:10.431
‎Did the procedure go well that day?

607
31:10.515 --> 31:12.225
‎Dr. Bae is a good teacher, so yes.

608
31:13.393 --> 31:14.644
‎That's a relief.

609
31:14.727 --> 31:16.813
‎I was afraid he was too angry to focus.

610
31:17.397 --> 31:19.607
‎He is short-tempered, ‎but he knows when to focus.

611
31:21.317 --> 31:22.568
‎You're an outcast intern, aren't you?

612
31:22.652 --> 31:23.569
‎Me?

613
31:24.112 --> 31:26.114
‎No, not at all. I have a lot of friends.

614
31:26.197 --> 31:27.573
‎What friends?

615
31:28.950 --> 31:29.951
‎From high school.

616
31:32.578 --> 31:35.289
‎You know how busy interns are.

617
31:36.165 --> 31:39.043
‎The interns in my department ‎meet up and eat together.

618
31:41.212 --> 31:42.046
‎I see.

619
31:43.715 --> 31:45.466
‎I'm focusing on my studies…

620
31:47.760 --> 31:49.095
‎I guess I shouldn't tell lies.

621
31:52.390 --> 31:54.559
‎Are you worried about Dr. Gye ‎because she's an outcast too?

622
31:54.642 --> 31:57.186
‎That's not true. ‎Dr. Gye and I aren't outcasts.

623
31:58.021 --> 32:00.732
‎You don't perform surgery alone. ‎It's a team effort.

624
32:01.232 --> 32:03.401
‎You need to know ‎how to fit in and get along.

625
32:03.484 --> 32:05.028
‎Sometimes, you need to hold back

626
32:05.111 --> 32:06.779
‎and just smile even when you're pissed.

627
32:06.863 --> 32:08.865
‎Right, "rage-smile."

628
32:10.158 --> 32:11.826
‎How'd you know I have low BP?

629
32:12.660 --> 32:14.245
‎You've got a gift for spiking it.

630
32:15.246 --> 32:17.165
‎This is really good. Try a bite.

631
32:17.248 --> 32:19.375
‎Hey, I took pity on you ‎and your clueless fool vibe.

632
32:19.459 --> 32:21.669
‎Me? A clueless fool? No way.

633
32:24.422 --> 32:27.216
‎Dr. Jo, I have a question.

634
32:28.342 --> 32:31.054
‎This hospital has ‎ten neurosurgeons on staff.

635
32:31.137 --> 32:33.097
‎Even if doctors who can do ‎a craniotomy are rare…

636
32:34.015 --> 32:35.683
‎I mean, we've got so many hospital beds.

637
32:35.767 --> 32:37.518
‎Why not bring in more neurosurgeons?

638
32:38.019 --> 32:39.562
‎It comes down to money.

639
32:39.645 --> 32:42.648
‎You think there are more patients ‎with appendicitis or brain bleeds?

640
32:43.399 --> 32:44.692
‎Both are cheap, right?

641
32:44.776 --> 32:47.445
‎Then they'll choose the easier surgery. ‎They're getting peanuts anyway.

642
32:48.446 --> 32:50.281
‎They're focused on money-making surgeries.

643
32:50.364 --> 32:53.451
‎A hospital near GUMC ‎has less than 1,000 beds,

644
32:53.534 --> 32:56.370
‎but they have more doctors ‎who can treat brain bleeds.

645
32:56.454 --> 32:57.705
‎GUMC absolutely pales in comparison.

646
32:57.789 --> 32:58.915
‎So that's why

647
32:59.540 --> 33:01.834
‎-you assigned Su-jeong there? ‎-Of course.

648
33:02.418 --> 33:04.962
‎Hospitals obsessed with money ‎always crash and burn.

649
33:05.046 --> 33:06.714
‎They're bound to screw up.

650
33:08.424 --> 33:10.259
‎-I have a nose for that stuff. ‎-Oh, sure.

651
33:10.343 --> 33:12.261
‎If your nose is so amazing,

652
33:12.345 --> 33:15.223
‎why can't you sniff out a flat tire?

653
33:16.724 --> 33:19.560
‎Because screw-ups like that ‎smell like crap. Downright nasty.

654
33:23.856 --> 33:24.816
‎Is it on my face?

655
33:25.608 --> 33:26.442
‎Damn it.

656
33:27.151 --> 33:29.487
‎You know how many doctors nationwide ‎can do aneurysm clipping?

657
33:30.488 --> 33:32.281
‎Barely over 130.

658
33:32.907 --> 33:34.534
‎And most are in their sixties.

659
33:35.535 --> 33:38.579
‎Hardly anyone wants to teach it ‎or learn it anymore.

660
33:38.663 --> 33:40.289
‎They're on the brink of extinction.

661
33:41.541 --> 33:45.169
‎But in some cases, ‎aneurysm clipping is the only option.

662
33:45.253 --> 33:46.504
‎What then?

663
33:59.350 --> 34:00.184
‎Ma'am?

664
34:01.602 --> 34:03.062
‎Ma'am, are you okay?

665
34:04.730 --> 34:06.274
‎Can you get up?

666
34:07.275 --> 34:08.192
‎Ma'am, are you…

667
34:10.987 --> 34:12.155
‎Mr. Seo, are you okay?

668
34:12.238 --> 34:13.156
‎Mr. Seo?

669
34:15.074 --> 34:16.742
‎Then you'd better pray one of those 130

670
34:16.826 --> 34:19.370
‎is at the hospital you're taken to.

671
34:20.246 --> 34:22.206
‎I need some help here!

672
34:22.290 --> 34:24.208
‎Help me examine this patient!

673
34:37.847 --> 34:39.682
‎ENERGY DRINK

674
34:49.192 --> 34:51.777
‎-How long until Dr. Hwang gets here? ‎-About 40 to 50 minutes.

675
34:51.861 --> 34:53.529
‎He's at a Seoul Medical Association ‎meeting, but the traffic…

676
34:53.613 --> 34:55.907
‎And Dr. Jang? The Ulsan conference ‎ended yesterday morning.

677
34:56.574 --> 35:00.119
‎He used the opportunity ‎to go on a family trip.

678
35:00.203 --> 35:01.662
‎He's on his way, but…

679
35:01.746 --> 35:04.207
‎Is he trying to be Father of the Year?

680
35:10.129 --> 35:12.506
‎It's an SAH ‎secondary to a ruptured aneurysm.

681
35:12.590 --> 35:13.674
‎How about coiling?

682
35:13.758 --> 35:15.509
‎It's too difficult for now.

683
35:15.593 --> 35:17.011
‎She's conscious.

684
35:17.094 --> 35:20.056
‎She's complaining of pain and convulsing, ‎but she's conscious.

685
35:20.139 --> 35:21.599
‎-Transfer her now. ‎-No.

686
35:22.642 --> 35:24.560
‎We must treat her here no matter what.

687
35:24.644 --> 35:27.063
‎Ms. Lee, look around. ‎There's no one available.

688
35:27.146 --> 35:28.564
‎Then we'll wait for them.

689
35:28.648 --> 35:30.650
‎What? What are you talking about?

690
35:30.733 --> 35:33.486
‎Let's say we transferred ‎another staff member who collapsed here.

691
35:34.320 --> 35:36.364
‎If she dies,

692
35:36.447 --> 35:37.573
‎all hell will break loose.

693
35:37.657 --> 35:39.825
‎But she'll die if she waits here.

694
35:39.909 --> 35:42.078
‎I don't know much about medicine.

695
35:42.161 --> 35:45.665
‎But what I do know ‎is that the closest hospital

696
35:45.748 --> 35:47.833
‎where we can transfer her ‎for aneurysm clipping

697
35:47.917 --> 35:50.920
‎is Daeseok Hospital, ‎which is 50 minutes away.

698
35:51.003 --> 35:52.004
‎What do you mean?

699
35:52.088 --> 35:53.923
‎Dr. Nam at Junggyeong is 20 minutes away.

700
35:54.006 --> 35:55.341
‎Dr. Nam went into private practice.

701
35:55.424 --> 35:58.552
‎-They quit because it was too hard. ‎-Damn it.

702
35:59.887 --> 36:03.933
‎If we factor in morning traffic, ‎it'll take an hour even for an ambulance.

703
36:04.016 --> 36:06.143
‎It's the same amount of time to do either!

704
36:06.227 --> 36:08.646
‎This is a race against time. ‎Get her ready for transfer.

705
36:08.729 --> 36:10.273
‎Our hospital can't handle it.

706
36:10.356 --> 36:12.275
‎We have someone who can operate.

707
36:13.609 --> 36:14.485
‎Who is it?

708
36:16.779 --> 36:17.613
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon.

709
36:20.700 --> 36:23.995
‎I've reviewed a lot of your surgical cases ‎and related materials.

710
36:24.829 --> 36:25.913
‎I'm begging you.

711
36:27.373 --> 36:29.959
‎The director isn't prepared ‎to perform surgery--

712
36:30.042 --> 36:32.586
‎Since when do doctors ‎need to be prepared for surgery?

713
36:34.088 --> 36:36.757
‎I haven't operated in a very long time.

714
36:36.841 --> 36:38.968
‎I'll assist you, sir.

715
36:39.927 --> 36:42.305
‎You've done this surgery almost 300 times.

716
36:42.388 --> 36:43.764
‎-What are you doing? ‎-First,

717
36:44.849 --> 36:46.350
‎-let's review the materials-- ‎-No.

718
36:46.434 --> 36:47.852
‎You're the only one, sir.

719
36:48.436 --> 36:51.939
‎The only person in a 30-minute radius ‎who can do this surgery

720
36:52.023 --> 36:53.149
‎is you, Director Bu.

721
37:01.115 --> 37:02.074
‎Listen up.

722
37:02.158 --> 37:03.909
‎We're transferring this patient.

723
37:04.535 --> 37:07.413
‎-Prep an ambulance and call Daeseok. ‎-Yes, sir.

724
37:07.496 --> 37:08.497
‎You can't do that now!

725
37:09.206 --> 37:10.124
‎The surgery has begun.

726
37:19.300 --> 37:22.636
‎I paged Dr. Jo from Anesthesia ‎and secured an OR.

727
37:22.720 --> 37:24.347
‎Who the hell is operating?

728
37:26.474 --> 37:27.516
‎Dr. Gye, sir.

729
37:27.600 --> 37:28.601
‎-What? ‎-What?

730
37:31.854 --> 37:34.023
‎Craniotomy and aneurysm neck clipping.

731
37:34.982 --> 37:36.108
‎Let's begin.

732
37:37.401 --> 37:41.238
‎But Dr. Gye isn't board-certified ‎in neurosurgery.

733
37:42.365 --> 37:43.240
‎Doctor X…

734
37:44.325 --> 37:46.118
‎Dr. Do, we can't allow this.

735
37:47.745 --> 37:49.622
‎We must stop this surgery right now, sir.

736
38:06.722 --> 38:08.933
‎They can't do this. Damn it.

737
38:09.934 --> 38:11.602
‎Vitals are stable.

738
38:11.685 --> 38:12.812
‎Lidocaine.

739
38:12.895 --> 38:13.938
‎LIDOCAINE: LOCAL ANESTHETIC

740
38:39.296 --> 38:40.131
‎Scalpel.

741
38:50.516 --> 38:51.517
‎Raney clip.

742
38:57.314 --> 38:58.232
‎Sorry.

743
38:58.315 --> 39:00.401
‎I'm only calling to ask for a favor.

744
39:01.193 --> 39:03.904
‎You're going to have to ‎send the email out ASAP.

745
39:05.197 --> 39:07.324
‎I know. I should've had something ready.

746
39:08.159 --> 39:10.077
‎Well, you know how it is.

747
39:10.161 --> 39:11.620
‎Some people just won't buy it

748
39:11.704 --> 39:14.248
‎even when it's right there, ‎staring them in the face.

749
39:15.791 --> 39:17.793
‎Oh, great. I owe you big.

750
39:19.795 --> 39:21.255
‎Who gave her permission to operate?

751
39:21.338 --> 39:23.132
‎She doesn't need permission.

752
39:23.215 --> 39:24.675
‎If the patient is sick, you operate.

753
39:25.259 --> 39:27.803
‎Does she know how to perform this surgery?

754
39:30.222 --> 39:32.766
‎Director, is she doing it correctly?

755
39:33.517 --> 39:34.518
‎Yes.

756
39:34.602 --> 39:36.437
‎She's doing it perfectly.

757
39:37.021 --> 39:38.022
‎Jeez…

758
39:39.440 --> 39:41.233
‎This is insane.

759
39:41.317 --> 39:44.987
‎She's obsessed with surgeries ‎when she's not even board-certified.

760
39:47.114 --> 39:49.658
‎Dr. Do, you can't stop the surgery.

761
39:49.742 --> 39:51.243
‎-Huh? ‎-What the hell are you doing?

762
39:51.327 --> 39:53.537
‎Dr. Gye said she knows how to perform it.

763
39:53.621 --> 39:54.455
‎She can do it.

764
39:54.538 --> 39:56.040
‎How the hell do you know?

765
39:56.123 --> 39:57.208
‎I just do.

766
39:57.291 --> 39:59.293
‎If I can see it, surely you do too.

767
39:59.376 --> 40:00.711
‎You've seen what she can do.

768
40:00.794 --> 40:02.463
‎And you're watching right now.

769
40:02.546 --> 40:03.589
‎You little…

770
40:03.672 --> 40:07.009
‎Whether we transfer or wait, ‎the patient will miss the golden hour.

771
40:07.092 --> 40:08.844
‎If either choice comes with a risk,

772
40:08.928 --> 40:11.263
‎and there's a doctor ‎who's capable and willing,

773
40:11.347 --> 40:12.723
‎we need to take a chance.

774
40:12.806 --> 40:14.016
‎Have all of you lost it?

775
40:14.099 --> 40:16.644
‎You think a doctor who isn't ‎board-certified in neuro can do this?

776
40:19.813 --> 40:20.648
‎Hey, Gye Su…

777
40:21.899 --> 40:22.733
‎What the heck?

778
40:24.568 --> 40:26.111
‎Why isn't this working?

779
40:27.530 --> 40:29.114
‎-I'm sorry, sir. ‎-Hey!

780
40:29.198 --> 40:30.241
‎Are you serious?

781
40:30.324 --> 40:32.910
‎-Come here! ‎-I'm sorry!

782
40:35.412 --> 40:36.789
‎I'll go and tell her myself.

783
40:42.503 --> 40:43.712
‎Good morning, Director.

784
40:44.838 --> 40:45.881
‎I brought

785
40:46.715 --> 40:48.509
‎Dr. Gye's neurosurgery board certificate.

786
40:48.592 --> 40:50.553
‎-What? ‎-Neurosurgery?

787
40:50.636 --> 40:51.971
‎Neurosurgery? No way.

788
40:54.306 --> 40:55.307
‎Is that real?

789
40:55.391 --> 40:56.976
‎You still can't let her, sir.

790
40:57.560 --> 40:58.686
‎Periosteal elevator.

791
40:58.769 --> 41:01.438
‎PERIOSTEAL ELEVATOR: USED TO SEPARATE ‎THE PERIOSTEUM COVERING THE BONE

792
41:07.570 --> 41:08.946
‎-Let go, you punk! ‎-Hey!

793
41:09.029 --> 41:10.698
‎What do you think you're doing?

794
41:10.781 --> 41:11.907
‎-You're fired, Park. ‎-What?

795
41:11.991 --> 41:14.285
‎How dare you ‎cut communication with the OR?

796
41:14.368 --> 41:15.995
‎-Wait a minute! ‎-Give that to me!

797
41:16.078 --> 41:18.581
‎-Hey, stop! ‎-You think this place belongs to you?

798
41:18.664 --> 41:21.125
‎-Just wait a second! ‎-Get over here!

799
41:22.293 --> 41:24.378
‎Clipping. Fishhook, please.

800
41:36.307 --> 41:37.891
‎If we fail,

801
41:37.975 --> 41:41.020
‎this patient will die at the workplace ‎she cleaned every day.

802
41:41.687 --> 41:43.522
‎Her touch is everywhere in this hospital.

803
41:44.148 --> 41:44.982
‎Let's…

804
41:46.025 --> 41:47.067
‎give it our all.

805
41:47.651 --> 41:48.569
‎-Yes, ma'am. ‎-Yes, ma'am.

806
41:49.153 --> 41:50.446
‎Burr hole trephination.

807
41:50.529 --> 41:53.115
‎BURR HOLE TREPHINATION: SURGICAL PROCEDURE ‎TO DRILL A SMALL HOLE IN THE SKULL

808
41:53.741 --> 41:55.743
‎Dr. Gye already knew.

809
41:56.577 --> 41:58.245
‎She knew the patient would collapse.

810
41:58.329 --> 42:00.247
‎Huh? What are you talking about?

811
42:00.331 --> 42:02.207
‎She was sleeping in the ER at dawn.

812
42:03.042 --> 42:05.127
‎I think she was waiting for this patient.

813
42:07.463 --> 42:08.297
‎Director.

814
42:08.380 --> 42:11.133
‎I don't trust that certificate. ‎Let's go down there.

815
42:12.343 --> 42:13.302
‎Dr. Park.

816
42:13.385 --> 42:16.221
‎You're really going to pay for this.

817
42:16.305 --> 42:17.181
‎Understand?

818
42:18.057 --> 42:20.309
‎That's what I thought too, at first.

819
42:20.392 --> 42:22.269
‎But when I look at the monitor,

820
42:23.395 --> 42:24.605
‎I get what Dr. Park meant.

821
42:25.272 --> 42:27.149
‎Who on earth is that doctor?

822
43:11.527 --> 43:12.361
‎Clip.

823
43:14.905 --> 43:16.115
‎She found the neck already?

824
43:16.615 --> 43:17.574
‎This quickly?

825
43:18.659 --> 43:19.618
‎That's impossible.

826
43:21.328 --> 43:22.371
‎Clipping.

827
43:39.555 --> 43:42.015
‎Clipping successful.

828
43:44.977 --> 43:45.811
‎Bipolar forceps.

829
43:51.233 --> 43:52.693
‎Dr. Gye Su-jeong!

830
44:03.620 --> 44:06.832
‎Dr. Gye, today's lunch menu ‎is braised short ribs!

831
44:06.915 --> 44:08.208
‎I'll save a seat for you!

832
44:08.292 --> 44:09.960
‎Great job!

833
44:10.043 --> 44:11.086
‎Goodness.

834
44:18.427 --> 44:19.928
‎OPERATION TIME, TIME, ANESTHESIA TIME

835
44:29.062 --> 44:29.897
‎Good job, everyone.

836
44:29.980 --> 44:31.774
‎-Good job. ‎-Good job.

837
45:24.284 --> 45:26.995
‎What are the odds of her bleeding ‎or collapsing again?

838
45:27.579 --> 45:29.623
‎The surgery went perfectly.

839
45:30.874 --> 45:32.334
‎I haven't seen one like this in a while.

840
45:32.918 --> 45:34.002
‎Does that mean

841
45:34.086 --> 45:36.672
‎this will actually work ‎in our hospital's favor?

842
45:36.755 --> 45:37.714
‎Yes.

843
45:38.924 --> 45:40.217
‎I believe so.

844
45:43.679 --> 45:44.805
‎Let's talk outside.

845
46:02.864 --> 46:06.660
‎THIS SEAT IS RESERVED! ‎WILL BE OCCUPIED SHORTLY

846
46:31.310 --> 46:34.271
‎THIS SEAT IS RESERVED ‎THANK YOU FOR YOUR UNDERSTANDING

847
46:34.354 --> 46:37.274
‎RESERVED SEAT ‎THIS SEAT HAS BEEN SAVED

848
46:37.357 --> 46:39.484
‎I was at the Medical Association ‎Emergency Response Committee.

849
46:39.568 --> 46:42.487
‎Why didn't you come right back ‎after the conference?

850
46:42.571 --> 46:44.865
‎I tacked on a few vacation days ‎to my business trip.

851
46:44.948 --> 46:47.034
‎You're the one who suddenly went ‎to the Medical Association.

852
46:47.117 --> 46:49.745
‎How could I not go? ‎It was the Emergency Response Committee!

853
46:49.828 --> 46:51.830
‎Everyone's out to get doctors right now.

854
46:51.913 --> 46:52.956
‎Of course, I had to go!

855
46:53.040 --> 46:55.167
‎That's enough.

856
46:55.250 --> 46:56.960
‎We didn't gather to play the blame game.

857
46:59.671 --> 47:00.922
‎Dr. Jo.

858
47:01.006 --> 47:02.466
‎I didn't expect this from you.

859
47:02.549 --> 47:04.718
‎You'll open an OR to just anyone, huh?

860
47:04.801 --> 47:07.220
‎Is this reverse discrimination? ‎You only open ORs for women?

861
47:07.304 --> 47:11.183
‎Even if you were a woman, ‎I wouldn't have said yes to that chart.

862
47:11.266 --> 47:12.142
‎What?

863
47:12.225 --> 47:14.728
‎Dr. Jo, even if it was ‎an emergency surgery,

864
47:14.811 --> 47:16.063
‎we were in a conference.

865
47:16.146 --> 47:19.107
‎What's the point of a conference ‎that just wastes time?

866
47:19.691 --> 47:23.153
‎Wow, there's no sense of discipline ‎or order anymore.

867
47:23.236 --> 47:24.655
‎You're all lax

868
47:24.738 --> 47:26.823
‎and talking back to your seniors.

869
47:26.907 --> 47:30.035
‎Director, you should've waited for us.

870
47:30.118 --> 47:31.870
‎Then the patient would've died!

871
47:33.330 --> 47:34.539
‎What?

872
47:35.123 --> 47:36.375
‎That patient was lucky.

873
47:36.458 --> 47:38.460
‎She collapsed in a hospital ‎and was conscious.

874
47:38.543 --> 47:40.337
‎And there was an excellent doctor nearby.

875
47:41.213 --> 47:43.382
‎-Maybe if Mr. Seo-- ‎-Dr. Kim.

876
47:44.966 --> 47:46.677
‎That's enough. Why bring that up?

877
47:47.636 --> 47:49.179
‎It was you, wasn't it?

878
47:49.262 --> 47:51.264
‎The anonymous whistleblower.

879
47:53.475 --> 47:57.187
‎He was a longtime co-worker, ‎and the ER is a war zone.

880
47:57.270 --> 47:59.106
‎I'm sure you shared strong camaraderie.

881
48:00.148 --> 48:01.900
‎We left out doctors on purpose.

882
48:02.484 --> 48:06.113
‎The EMTs and nurses had ‎more damaging stories they could leak,

883
48:06.196 --> 48:09.616
‎so we preemptively scared everyone ‎with the internal investigation.

884
48:14.329 --> 48:15.497
‎That's right.

885
48:15.580 --> 48:16.623
‎I wrote the post.

886
48:17.416 --> 48:18.250
‎Dr. Kim.

887
48:18.750 --> 48:20.293
‎How could you?

888
48:20.377 --> 48:22.129
‎Do you know what I went through?

889
48:22.212 --> 48:24.131
‎Everyone around me ‎lost their minds over it!

890
48:24.214 --> 48:27.092
‎Director, we must bring Dr. Kim ‎before the ethics committee.

891
48:27.759 --> 48:30.721
‎Dr. Jang and I suffered greatly back then.

892
48:31.263 --> 48:32.180
‎Why did you write it?

893
48:33.932 --> 48:34.850
‎Mr. Seo…

894
48:36.184 --> 48:37.853
‎had a one-year-old daughter.

895
48:38.687 --> 48:41.356
‎She no longer has a father.

896
48:42.149 --> 48:43.525
‎Yes, I wrote it.

897
48:43.608 --> 48:45.026
‎They said it was nobody's fault.

898
48:45.527 --> 48:48.321
‎They blamed his illness, ‎his destiny, and his fate.

899
48:48.405 --> 48:49.865
‎They said he would've died anyway.

900
48:49.948 --> 48:53.410
‎Every doctor kept talking crap like that.

901
48:53.493 --> 48:56.079
‎That's why I got angry and wrote it.

902
48:56.163 --> 48:58.290
‎How could you say that ‎in front of the director?

903
48:58.373 --> 49:01.334
‎Since I'm not allowed to talk about it, ‎I had to write about it at least!

904
49:01.418 --> 49:03.253
‎His ICP was so high, ‎the contrast wouldn't flow,

905
49:03.336 --> 49:04.963
‎so we couldn't even coil him.

906
49:05.672 --> 49:09.009
‎Performing a craniotomy right then ‎wouldn't have helped.

907
49:09.092 --> 49:10.343
‎You know that.

908
49:10.427 --> 49:13.346
‎Are you saying the hospital ‎has no responsibility at all?

909
49:14.514 --> 49:17.058
‎You're just going to talk about ‎reimbursement rates?

910
49:17.142 --> 49:20.479
‎Are we seriously reducing this ‎to Mr. Seo's fate?

911
49:20.562 --> 49:22.481
‎Are you saying we're at fault then?

912
49:22.564 --> 49:24.608
‎How were we to know ‎he was going to get that sick?

913
49:25.192 --> 49:28.570
‎Do we have to live in this hospital ‎around the clock?

914
49:28.653 --> 49:30.238
‎Is that what we should do?

915
49:30.822 --> 49:32.073
‎Doctors are people too!

916
49:33.074 --> 49:33.909
‎Look…

917
49:42.292 --> 49:44.169
‎Who called Dr. Gye here?

918
49:45.921 --> 49:47.130
‎Hey, Dr. Gye.

919
49:47.672 --> 49:49.633
‎We'll talk to you separately, so leave.

920
49:51.760 --> 49:52.677
‎You're not the only one.

921
49:54.137 --> 49:55.764
‎Patients are people too.

922
49:57.599 --> 49:58.725
‎What?

923
49:58.809 --> 50:00.310
‎Did she just…

924
50:00.977 --> 50:02.771
‎Did you speak informally to me?

925
50:07.025 --> 50:07.859
‎So?

926
50:09.319 --> 50:11.863
‎Do you make an effort to be a doctor?

927
50:11.947 --> 50:12.781
‎Sir?

928
50:13.532 --> 50:15.867
‎Or are you just a person?

929
50:15.951 --> 50:19.120
‎Then when do you step up as a doctor?

930
50:19.996 --> 50:21.540
‎Only when you clock in?

931
50:22.165 --> 50:23.333
‎Or when you're at the hospital?

932
50:24.125 --> 50:26.336
‎Or just sometimes?

933
50:26.419 --> 50:27.671
‎How dare you…

934
50:27.754 --> 50:30.131
‎How old are you? ‎Just how long have you been practicing?

935
50:30.215 --> 50:31.967
‎Watch what you say, please.

936
50:32.050 --> 50:32.926
‎Dr. Gye.

937
50:33.677 --> 50:35.262
‎Apologize to everyone here.

938
50:35.345 --> 50:37.055
‎Ms. Yeo Jeong-sun

939
50:37.889 --> 50:39.140
‎works a two-shift schedule.

940
50:39.224 --> 50:40.600
‎Today was her day off.

941
50:41.518 --> 50:44.062
‎But a co-worker's daughter ‎injured her back,

942
50:44.145 --> 50:46.523
‎so she came in as a favor ‎to her co-worker.

943
50:48.316 --> 50:49.276
‎Ms. Yeo

944
50:50.402 --> 50:52.571
‎was also in charge of ‎cleaning this office.

945
50:52.654 --> 50:54.656
‎It's a good thing she came to work then.

946
50:54.739 --> 50:56.575
‎Imagine if she'd been ‎outside or at home.

947
50:56.658 --> 50:58.785
‎See? She was meant to live.

948
50:58.869 --> 51:00.996
‎You shouldn't be saying things like that!

949
51:01.079 --> 51:04.124
‎She didn't come because she was ill. ‎She was ill, but still came to work!

950
51:04.207 --> 51:06.334
‎And luckily for her, ‎she collapsed in a hospital.

951
51:07.002 --> 51:09.546
‎So that's why the trash can is full.

952
51:09.629 --> 51:12.674
‎They should've sent a replacement. ‎How irresponsible.

953
51:13.174 --> 51:14.009
‎Dr. Jang!

954
51:14.092 --> 51:15.176
‎What?

955
51:17.053 --> 51:18.263
‎What are you doing?

956
51:18.346 --> 51:19.306
‎Dr. Gye!

957
51:19.389 --> 51:21.725
‎Stop making a scene and apologize now!

958
51:22.309 --> 51:24.394
‎Hey, are you that confident in yourself?

959
51:24.978 --> 51:27.772
‎This industry is a lot smaller ‎than you think.

960
51:27.856 --> 51:30.275
‎Your career can be over in a heartbeat.

961
51:30.358 --> 51:32.777
‎Why the hell did you hire her, Ms. Lee?

962
51:32.861 --> 51:35.405
‎I guarantee that within the next few days,

963
51:35.488 --> 51:37.532
‎it'll rupture, ‎or another issue will occur.

964
51:37.616 --> 51:39.659
‎I'll bet my white coat on this!

965
51:39.743 --> 51:40.994
‎I will too.

966
51:41.077 --> 51:43.538
‎Let's see what happens. ‎How confident are you now?

967
51:43.622 --> 51:45.123
‎You think she would've pulled it off?

968
51:45.206 --> 51:47.500
‎Can you guarantee she didn't fail?

969
51:48.710 --> 51:50.003
‎Are you confident?

970
51:50.086 --> 51:52.672
‎Can you guarantee it won't rupture ‎or cause any other issue?

971
51:52.756 --> 51:55.383
‎Please give us an OR, Dr. Jo. ‎We're counting on you.

972
51:55.467 --> 51:58.053
‎I can't let her into an OR. ‎She's not board-certified in neuro.

973
51:58.136 --> 51:59.554
‎-Absolutely not. ‎-What if I am?

974
52:01.056 --> 52:02.140
‎What did you say?

975
52:02.766 --> 52:04.601
‎You know I'll pull it off.

976
52:05.435 --> 52:08.480
‎-There's no time. We have to-- ‎-I'm reporting this to Director Bu.

977
52:09.189 --> 52:10.774
‎You said so yourself.

978
52:10.857 --> 52:12.108
‎In cases like this,

979
52:12.192 --> 52:15.028
‎you need to pray one of those 130 ‎is at that hospital.

980
52:15.904 --> 52:18.782
‎Dr. Jo, that one out of 130 is right here.

981
52:18.865 --> 52:20.158
‎She's right in front of us.

982
52:20.241 --> 52:21.493
‎Please, Dr. Jo.

983
52:21.576 --> 52:24.454
‎That patient is ‎one of the hospital's cleaning staff.

984
52:24.537 --> 52:28.083
‎She's probably cleaned ‎the very phone you're holding.

985
52:31.211 --> 52:32.087
‎Park Tae-gyeong.

986
52:32.963 --> 52:33.797
‎Listen carefully.

987
52:34.839 --> 52:35.924
‎What matters more is

988
52:36.007 --> 52:38.885
‎what kind of doctor ‎that one-in-130 actually is.

989
52:38.969 --> 52:40.637
‎Is it someone who just knows how to do it?

990
52:40.720 --> 52:43.682
‎Or someone who can perform the surgery ‎with precision every step of the way?

991
52:47.560 --> 52:48.436
‎I…

992
52:49.980 --> 52:51.773
‎don't ever fail.

993
52:56.861 --> 52:58.238
‎Get ready to lose your white coats.

994
52:59.072 --> 53:01.282
‎Where are you going? Stop right there!

995
53:02.701 --> 53:05.870
‎You give me shit if I stay, ‎and give me shit if I leave…

996
53:07.080 --> 53:07.914
‎"Give you shit"?

997
53:09.165 --> 53:10.667
‎Did I hear that right?

998
53:10.750 --> 53:13.545
‎Director, fire her right now.

999
53:13.628 --> 53:15.839
‎She's toxic to the hospital ‎and undermines discipline.

1000
53:15.922 --> 53:18.091
‎We need to ban her from medicine!

1001
53:18.174 --> 53:19.175
‎Enough!

1002
53:23.430 --> 53:24.472
‎Don't you have any shame?

1003
53:25.181 --> 53:27.183
‎You hold people accountable ‎over a damn trash can.

1004
53:27.267 --> 53:29.811
‎But when a life is on the line, ‎why won't any of you…

1005
53:32.230 --> 53:33.440
‎Why on earth…

1006
53:34.983 --> 53:36.067
‎does no one…

1007
53:46.786 --> 53:47.954
‎You haven't gone in yet?

1008
53:48.788 --> 53:51.082
‎No, the meeting is ‎taking longer than expected.

1009
53:58.298 --> 53:59.215
‎I'm sorry.

1010
54:00.800 --> 54:02.385
‎-About what? ‎-"About what?"

1011
54:03.428 --> 54:04.679
‎Do I have a lot to be sorry for?

1012
54:05.263 --> 54:07.223
‎Do you mean in the observation gallery?

1013
54:07.307 --> 54:09.142
‎No, I'm talking about in front of the OR

1014
54:09.225 --> 54:12.270
‎when I lost my temper ‎and poked you in the chest.

1015
54:12.353 --> 54:13.855
‎Oh, that?

1016
54:13.938 --> 54:14.939
‎You know,

1017
54:16.399 --> 54:18.485
‎you have a way ‎of pushing people's buttons.

1018
54:18.568 --> 54:19.819
‎I was wrong too.

1019
54:19.903 --> 54:22.655
‎I crossed the line, and I'm sorry.

1020
54:23.490 --> 54:25.450
‎I got ahead of myself.

1021
54:25.533 --> 54:26.785
‎It was hard to accept

1022
54:26.868 --> 54:29.245
‎that the organization I chose ‎delivered an outcome that--

1023
54:29.329 --> 54:30.163
‎Forget it.

1024
54:30.663 --> 54:31.539
‎Look.

1025
54:32.749 --> 54:33.708
‎It's not that

1026
54:34.584 --> 54:36.086
‎I don't understand you…

1027
54:41.925 --> 54:43.301
‎But you're just an intern,

1028
54:43.384 --> 54:45.220
‎so finish your monthly rotation and go.

1029
54:45.303 --> 54:47.514
‎A lot of interns do a surgery rotation

1030
54:47.597 --> 54:50.600
‎so they can act all dedicated, ‎but they end up going somewhere else.

1031
54:51.726 --> 54:53.228
‎I'm done watching that happen.

1032
54:55.105 --> 54:56.773
‎You won't choose general surgery anyway.

1033
55:02.112 --> 55:02.987
‎There you are.

1034
55:03.696 --> 55:05.406
‎Why are you by yourself? ‎Where's the intern?

1035
55:06.074 --> 55:07.408
‎Why did you come alone?

1036
55:07.492 --> 55:10.328
‎Then what should I do?

1037
55:11.996 --> 55:13.331
‎What kind of doctor should I be?

1038
55:14.541 --> 55:16.835
‎Can I even be a doctor?

1039
55:17.335 --> 55:19.712
‎Tell Park Tae-gyeong or whatever ‎to get in here now!

1040
55:19.796 --> 55:22.298
‎This is all because of that damn intern…

1041
55:23.299 --> 55:26.302
‎Never mind being a doctor. I'm dead meat.

1042
56:16.978 --> 56:19.230
‎Thank you for taking the time to join us.

1043
56:20.607 --> 56:22.358
‎I'm Bu Seung-gwon,

1044
56:22.442 --> 56:25.570
‎the new director ‎at Guseo University Seonam Medical Center.

1045
56:26.279 --> 56:29.490
‎I requested a press conference ‎and not an inauguration ceremony

1046
56:30.325 --> 56:32.994
‎because today marks the first anniversary

1047
56:33.995 --> 56:37.081
‎of the passing of Mr. Seo Jin-yeong, ‎who died while on duty last year.

1048
56:37.874 --> 56:39.918
‎As you may have recently heard,

1049
56:40.001 --> 56:42.795
‎we had another similar incident ‎at our hospital.

1050
56:44.339 --> 56:46.758
‎While on the job, ‎one of our cleaning staff

1051
56:47.717 --> 56:49.761
‎collapsed from a cerebral hemorrhage.

1052
56:49.844 --> 56:52.305
‎And our medical staff

1053
56:52.388 --> 56:54.724
‎did everything in their power ‎to treat her.

1054
56:55.516 --> 56:56.976
‎In the wake of this incident,

1055
56:58.228 --> 57:01.606
‎I intend to do ‎what the former director did not.

1056
57:02.857 --> 57:05.193
‎Mr. Seo Jin-yeong's death

1057
57:05.276 --> 57:08.821
‎exposed the deep flaws ‎in our medical system.

1058
57:09.405 --> 57:10.782
‎Absurd reimbursement rates,

1059
57:12.075 --> 57:14.577
‎chronic staffing shortages, ‎and insufficient budgets.

1060
57:15.203 --> 57:16.704
‎Yes, that's right.

1061
57:16.788 --> 57:18.164
‎All of this is true.

1062
57:18.248 --> 57:19.290
‎However,

1063
57:20.041 --> 57:21.626
‎it's also not the whole story.

1064
57:22.293 --> 57:23.211
‎Before all that,

1065
57:23.711 --> 57:27.090
‎a fundamental trust must exist ‎for everyone at our hospital.

1066
57:27.757 --> 57:30.718
‎All staff members ‎should be able to trust that

1067
57:31.553 --> 57:33.471
‎if they get injured or collapse ‎during their shift,

1068
57:33.555 --> 57:35.640
‎they'll get the proper care they need

1069
57:35.723 --> 57:40.478
‎to make it home safely ‎at the end of the day.

1070
57:41.688 --> 57:42.689
‎This hospital…

1071
57:44.357 --> 57:46.609
‎broke that trust.

1072
57:47.735 --> 57:48.987
‎So, for the first time,

1073
57:49.070 --> 57:52.240
‎to the late Mr. Seo's family, ‎to the public that we've disappointed,

1074
57:53.324 --> 57:56.327
‎and to all members of our hospital family,

1075
57:56.828 --> 57:59.789
‎I offer my deepest apologies.

1076
58:16.097 --> 58:17.140
‎I'll take questions now.

1077
58:21.811 --> 58:22.687
‎This is strange.

1078
58:22.770 --> 58:25.273
‎Kim Seong-jin didn't write that post.

1079
58:28.401 --> 58:29.485
‎You did.

1080
58:31.279 --> 58:33.072
‎I assume it was out of guilt

1081
58:34.198 --> 58:35.491
‎and a sense of responsibility.

1082
58:36.534 --> 58:38.453
‎You begged me for that footage,

1083
58:39.287 --> 58:41.205
‎saying things would change ‎if we exposed it.

1084
58:41.289 --> 58:42.665
‎You asked me to trust you.

1085
58:42.749 --> 58:43.750
‎So, has anything changed?

1086
58:53.926 --> 58:55.136
‎Let's just wait and see.

1087
58:56.220 --> 58:57.263
‎This is just the start.

1088
59:06.481 --> 59:11.069
‎The newly appointed director ‎at Guseo University Seonam Medical Center

1089
59:11.152 --> 59:14.447
‎is taking an unusual approach ‎to the death of EMT Seo Jin-yeong.

1090
59:14.530 --> 59:17.325
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon ‎bowed and apologized

1091
59:17.408 --> 59:19.285
‎for the previous leadership's mistakes

1092
59:19.369 --> 59:22.914
‎and stated he would cooperate fully ‎with the bereaved family's appeal.

1093
59:22.997 --> 59:27.418
‎He also expressed his desire ‎to speak directly with the family.

1094
59:27.960 --> 59:29.796
‎Hospital officials say

1095
59:29.879 --> 59:32.298
‎Director Bu Seung-gwon ‎requested a press conference

1096
59:32.382 --> 59:35.051
‎to state his position ‎rather than hold an inauguration ceremony.

1097
59:36.010 --> 59:39.222
‎Are you saying this is a new contract?

1098
59:39.305 --> 59:41.265
‎As you can see,

1099
59:41.974 --> 59:43.685
‎as a cerebrovascular neurosurgeon,

1100
59:43.768 --> 59:47.522
‎Dr. Gye possesses ‎exceptional surgical skills.

1101
59:48.731 --> 59:51.776
‎And she's already stepped in ‎to cover the hospital's staffing shortage.

1102
59:51.859 --> 59:54.821
‎Oh, I sent you ‎a separate invoice for that.

1103
59:54.904 --> 59:57.490
‎You're basically asking ‎for more money, right?

1104
59:57.990 --> 01:00:01.285
‎I believe this incident proves ‎that she's worth it.

1105
01:00:02.370 --> 01:00:03.955
‎And the other terms remain the same?

1106
01:00:04.038 --> 01:00:05.331
‎No, there's one more.

1107
01:00:05.415 --> 01:00:06.290
‎What is it?

1108
01:00:06.374 --> 01:00:08.626
‎I don't work in a department ‎I didn't choose.

1109
01:00:08.710 --> 01:00:10.294
‎How dare you? You're just a locum.

1110
01:00:10.837 --> 01:00:12.547
‎You go where you're told.

1111
01:00:24.559 --> 01:00:27.437
‎You're not on great terms ‎with the current administration.

1112
01:00:27.520 --> 01:00:29.856
‎And people are talking about ‎another strike.

1113
01:00:29.939 --> 01:00:33.443
‎What if a staffing shortage hits, ‎and there's a major accident?

1114
01:00:33.526 --> 01:00:36.696
‎Goodness, just thinking about it ‎gives me chills.

1115
01:00:37.613 --> 01:00:40.116
‎Who's going to fill that gap then?

1116
01:00:40.199 --> 01:00:42.410
‎Are you saying Dr. Gye will fill it?

1117
01:00:43.077 --> 01:00:45.246
‎Of course not. Money will fill the gap.

1118
01:00:45.830 --> 01:00:48.624
‎Even if this place is hanging by a thread,

1119
01:00:48.708 --> 01:00:51.002
‎it still belongs to a foundation ‎that brings in a net profit

1120
01:00:51.085 --> 01:00:52.420
‎of tens of billions of won per year.

1121
01:00:52.503 --> 01:00:55.006
‎Shouldn't you open your wallet for this?

1122
01:00:57.550 --> 01:00:59.552
‎Let's go over the terms and the rates.

1123
01:01:00.219 --> 01:01:01.804
‎First, the employment terms.

1124
01:01:01.888 --> 01:01:04.348
‎-"Working past regular hours--" ‎-Excuse me.

1125
01:01:10.605 --> 01:01:11.564
‎Escort him in.

1126
01:01:13.608 --> 01:01:14.442
‎He's here.

1127
01:01:15.109 --> 01:01:18.112
‎This is an important moment. ‎What's going on?

1128
01:01:28.414 --> 01:01:29.540
‎It's been a long time, sir.

1129
01:01:29.624 --> 01:01:30.625
‎How have you been?

1130
01:01:31.459 --> 01:01:32.585
‎You look good.

1131
01:01:33.336 --> 01:01:34.253
‎Take a seat.

1132
01:01:39.467 --> 01:01:42.178
‎Please say hello. This is…

1133
01:01:42.261 --> 01:01:43.221
‎I'm Na Dae-il.

1134
01:01:44.263 --> 01:01:46.307
‎I'm joining general surgery ‎starting today.

1135
01:01:47.183 --> 01:01:48.392
‎Nice to meet you.

1136
01:01:56.067 --> 01:01:57.902
‎The contract will be put on hold.

1137
01:02:08.996 --> 01:02:11.040
‎MEDICAL SERVICE RATE SHEET

1138
01:02:25.596 --> 01:02:28.432
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1139
01:03:07.555 --> 01:03:10.474
‎DOCTOR X: MAFIA IN WHITE

1140
01:03:10.558 --> 01:03:12.226
‎Is Dr. Na doing a fine job or what?

1141
01:03:12.310 --> 01:03:13.477
‎Shoulders back.

1142
01:03:13.561 --> 01:03:14.562
‎You're Gye Su-jeong.

1143
01:03:15.229 --> 01:03:16.230
‎Page the OR.

1144
01:03:16.314 --> 01:03:18.566
‎Why did you go into someone else's OR ‎and cause trouble?

1145
01:03:18.649 --> 01:03:20.735
‎I heard something happened ‎between you and Dr. Na.

1146
01:03:20.818 --> 01:03:22.695
‎That bastard's hands reek.

1147
01:03:22.778 --> 01:03:24.739
‎So? What about the surgery?

1148
01:03:24.822 --> 01:03:27.074
‎It's almost scary ‎how people are connected.

1149
01:03:27.158 --> 01:03:29.952
‎I'm curious to know ‎what you see ahead of you.

1150
01:03:30.703 --> 01:03:32.038
‎I only focus on what's ahead?

1151
01:03:33.039 --> 01:03:34.373
‎You seemed like a god.

1152
01:03:34.457 --> 01:03:35.499
‎Or a monster.

1153
01:03:36.542 --> 01:03:41.547
‎Subtitle translation by: Jenny Kim
